    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70458" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεόω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>renovate, change,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέωσον αἶνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					534
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.):— 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάφους ἐνεώσατο</span>
			<i>had</i> them <i>restored,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.1721
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεάω</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.221
			</span></i>: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεώσατε ἑαυτοῖς νεώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Je.</u>
					4.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>restore</i> a M<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> reading in a corrupt passage, <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.Lac.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1012.26
			</span></i>.</div>
